580	 * before its first "/" is a 20-64 character plain key and the rest is a path) is left to the bounded `sk-` patterns,
581	 * which stop at the "/".
582	 * Invariant: redaction only grows. The original run is always judged and kept; longer runs (through an encoded
583	 * "/" or "+", or a dotted continuation) are judged in addition and budgeted, so cost is linear on any input. Only a
584	 * key that starts past everything already scanned (`at >= scannedTo`) draws on the main budget, whose windows are
585	 * disjoint and so cannot exceed the text; a key inside an earlier window (a rescan) draws on a small separate quota.
